========================================================================
Part A: exact lower bound  F*_NS(S=4;N) >= ceil(N/4)/N  (all N)
========================================================================
  (min over all even-parity multisets; parity lemma gives >= ceil(N/4), round-robin attains)
  Monotonicity: S_NS(N,F) <= S_max(N,F) for every F, so
    {F : S_NS(N,F)>=4} subseteq {F : S_max(N,F)>=4}
    => F*_NS(S=4;N) = min{F:S_NS>=4} >= min{F:S_max>=4} = ceil(N/4)/N  (Theorem 2).
  Part A: PASS

